ISO 226:2023, Table 1
---------------------

The per-frequency coefficients in `iso226_utils.py` (`ISO_AF`, `ISO_LU` and
`ISO_TF`, 29 values each) are reproduced from Table 1 of

    ISO 226:2023, Acoustics -- Normal equal-loudness-level contours
    (c) International Organization for Standardization

They are reproduced because ISO 226 Formula (1) cannot be evaluated without
them: with those coefficients removed the software has no function.

**Permission for this reproduction has been requested and is pending.** ISO
customer service confirmed on 1 August 2026 that reproducing Table 1 requires
explicit permission or a licensing agreement, and that such permissions are
handled by the national ISO member body -- ANSI in the United States. A request
is with ANSI. If permission is refused, these coefficients will be removed and
this notice updated to say so.

Nothing else from the standard is reproduced here beyond short quotations of
the Scope and of the stated range of validity of Formula (1). Annex B is
deliberately excluded: it is used only to verify this implementation, the values
are not in this repository, and the test that uses them is disabled unless a
user supplies them from their own copy of the standard.

**This project is not a substitute for the standard.** Anyone doing serious work
with equal-loudness contours should buy it: https://www.iso.org/standard/83117.html


ISO 266
-------

`ISO_FREQ` is the preferred one-third-octave frequency series of ISO 266,
included so the coefficients above are correctly indexed.
